#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "I-simulate ang Bose-Hubbard dynamics na may mapipiling encoding para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit bosons"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding"
msgstr "I-simulate ang Bose-Hubbard dynamics na may mapipiling encoding"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-getting-started\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"
msgstr "I-simulate ang Bose-Hubbard dynamics na may mapipiling encoding {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Bose-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities against an exact reference. What makes the route interesting is a single idea:\n"
msgstr "Ang gabay na ito ay bumubuo ng Circuit para sa **time dynamics ng one-dimensional na Bose-Hubbard model**, mula sa pagsulat ng Hamiltonian hanggang sa pagsuri ng mga evolved na site density laban sa eksaktong reference. Ang dahilan kung bakit kawili-wili ang ruta ay isang ideya lang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Do not choose a boson-to-qubit encoding when you build the circuit. Build the circuit on **bosonic modes**, and let the **transpiler** decide how those modes become qubits.\n"
msgstr "> Huwag pumili ng boson-to-qubit encoding kapag binubuo mo ang Circuit. Buuin ang Circuit sa **bosonic modes**, at hayaan ang **Transpiler** na magpasya kung paano magiging mga qubit ang mga mode na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For bosons, you nearly always need to defer the encoding. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional and no encoding exists until you first pick a **truncation** $d$ (the number of occupation levels you keep). In code the truncation is given as the largest occupation a mode can hold, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, so a mode that keeps the levels $0, 1, 2$ has `max_occupation = 2` and $d = 3$.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga boson, halos palagi mong kailangang ipagpaliban ang encoding. Ang isang bosonic mode ay kayang maglaman ng kahit ilang particle, kaya ang Fock space nito ay infinite-dimensional at walang encoding hangga't hindi ka muna pumipili ng **truncation** $d$ (ang bilang ng mga occupation level na itatago mo). Sa code, ibinibigay ang truncation bilang pinakamalaking occupation na kayang hawakan ng isang mode, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, kaya ang isang mode na nagtatago ng mga level na $0, 1, 2$ ay may `max_occupation = 2` at $d = 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That makes the truncation a *parameter of the encoding*, not of the physics, and it is a parameter you want to vary: too small and the answer is wrong, too large and the circuit is needlessly wide. If you defer the encoding to transpile time, you can sweep the truncation without changing the circuit, the Hamiltonian, or the grouping.\n"
msgstr "Dahil dito, ang truncation ay *parameter ng encoding*, hindi ng physics, at ito ay parameter na gusto mong baguhin: kapag masyadong maliit, mali ang sagot, at kapag masyadong malaki, hindi kailangang lumapad ang Circuit. Kung ipagpapaliban mo ang encoding hanggang sa transpile time, maaari mong i-sweep ang truncation nang hindi binabago ang Circuit, ang Hamiltonian, o ang grouping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [operators guide](operators#operators-explanation) for the operator data structure, the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the encodings and the recipe for writing a custom mapper, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tingnan din\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang [gabay sa operators](operators#operators-explanation) para sa operator data structure, ang [gabay sa mappers](mappers#mappers-explanation) para sa mga encoding at ang recipe sa pagsulat ng custom mapper, at ang [gabay sa transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) para sa mga yugto ng Transpiler na tinutukoy sa buong gabay.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncation, and what it costs {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"
msgstr "Ang truncation, at ang halaga nito {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you truncate a mode to $d$ levels, you break the canonical commutator on the highest retained level <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), so no encoding is an isomorphism of *algebras*: a bosonic encoding maps states, and operators acting within the truncated subspace. Two consequences matter for everything that follows:\n"
msgstr "Kapag tinruncate mo ang isang mode sa $d$ na level, nasisira mo ang canonical commutator sa pinakamataas na level na itinago <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), kaya walang encoding na isomorphism ng mga *algebra*: ang isang bosonic encoding ay nagmamapa ng mga state, at mga operator na kumikilos sa loob ng truncated subspace. Dalawang bunga ang mahalaga sa lahat ng susunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$d$ must bound the occupation reachable by the dynamics, not merely that of the initial state.\n"
msgstr "Dapat na ang $d$ ang maglimita sa occupation na maaabot ng dynamics, hindi lang ng initial state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping does not commute with normal ordering, so decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and stay consistent.\n"
msgstr "Hindi nagko-commute ang mapping sa normal ordering, kaya magpasya nang minsanan kung ang Hamiltonian mo ay nakadefine sa normal-ordered na anyo, at manatiling pare-pareho.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [mappers guide](mappers#truncation-explanation) derives the defect and shows both consequences on running code.\n"
msgstr "Ang [gabay sa mappers](mappers#truncation-explanation) ang naghahango ng depekto at nagpapakita ng parehong bunga sa tumatakbong code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Ang Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Bose-Hubbard model on a lattice with bonds $\\langle i j \\rangle$ is\n"
msgstr "Ang Bose-Hubbard model sa isang lattice na may mga bond na $\\langle i j \\rangle$ ay\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. The interaction counts *pairs* of bosons on a site, so it requires a site to hold two particles at once. Normal-ordered, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which is the form used in what follows.\n"
msgstr "na may $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. Binibilang ng interaksyon ang mga *pares* ng boson sa isang site, kaya kailangang magkaroon ang site ng dalawang particle nang sabay. Kapag normal-ordered, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, na siyang anyong gagamitin sa susunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The geometry enters only through the edge list, so nothing is specific to a chain:\n"
msgstr "Sa edge list lang pumapasok ang geometry, kaya walang anumang partikular sa isang chain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two properties are worth checking first. The Hamiltonian must be Hermitian for $e^{-itH}$ to be unitary, and it conserves the total boson number:\n"
msgstr "Dalawang katangian ang dapat munang suriin. Dapat Hermitian ang Hamiltonian para maging unitary ang $e^{-itH}$, at iniingatan nito ang kabuuang bilang ng boson:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the bosonic question: how many levels does this operator demand?\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, ang tanong tungkol sa boson: ilang level ang hinihingi ng operator na ito?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interaction term applies two creation operators to one mode, so a mode has to hold two bosons for the term to act at all. That is a **maximum occupation** of 2, which is the number that [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") takes as its `max_occupation`. A mode that keeps the occupations $0, 1, 2$ has $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ levels, so `max_occupation >= 2` is the same requirement as $d \\geq 3$.\n"
msgstr "Ang interaction term ay naglalapat ng dalawang creation operator sa isang mode, kaya kailangang magkaroon ang mode ng dalawang boson para gumana ang term. Iyon ay **maximum occupation** na 2, na siyang numerong tinatanggap ng [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") bilang `max_occupation` nito. Ang isang mode na nagtatago ng mga occupation na $0, 1, 2$ ay may $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ na level, kaya ang `max_occupation >= 2` ay kapareho ng requirement na $d \\geq 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a lower bound only: it comes from one application of the operator, and repeated application over a time evolution can reach further. It rules out cutoffs that are certainly too small, and step 6 settles, for this model and state, how large the cutoff has to be. [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") reports the bound for each mode separately, which is what a per-mode cutoff is compared against.\n"
msgstr "Lower bound lang ito: nagmumula ito sa isang paglalapat ng operator, at ang paulit-ulit na paglalapat sa buong time evolution ay maaaring umabot nang mas malayo. Inaalis nito ang mga cutoff na tiyak na masyadong maliit, at ang hakbang 6 ang magsasabi, para sa model at state na ito, kung gaano kalaki dapat ang cutoff. Iniuulat ng [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") ang bound para sa bawat mode nang hiwalay, na siyang ikinukumpara sa cutoff kada mode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"group-before-mapping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-grouping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Group before mapping {#2-group-before-mapping}"
msgstr "2. Mag-group bago mag-map {#2-group-before-mapping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The evolution is Trotterized, and how the Hamiltonian is partitioned decides what the synthesis is handed. Two considerations pull in the same direction.\n"
msgstr "Trotterized ang evolution, at ang paraan ng paghahati ng Hamiltonian ang nagpapasya kung ano ang ibibigay sa synthesis. Dalawang konsiderasyon ang nagtutulak sa iisang direksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, a physical one: the individual hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is **not Hermitian**. Only the pair $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ is. If you evolve under a single non-Hermitian term, the operation is not unitary, and the mapped operator would carry complex coefficients that [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects. Each bond’s two hopping terms must therefore stay together.\n"
msgstr "Una, isang pisikal: ang indibidwal na hopping term na $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ ay **hindi Hermitian**. Ang pares lang na $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ ang Hermitian. Kung ie-evolve mo sa ilalim ng iisang non-Hermitian na term, hindi unitary ang operasyon, at ang na-map na operator ay magkakaroon ng mga complex coefficient na tinatanggihan ng [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). Kaya dapat manatiling magkasama ang dalawang hopping term ng bawat bond.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, an efficiency one: all the on-site interaction terms are diagonal in the occupation basis and mutually commute, so they can share a single group and be synthesized together. The same holds for the bonds that touch no common site. On a chain, every second bond is such a set: bonds 0 and 2 act on disjoint pairs of modes, so their hopping terms commute and can share a group, and bond 1 forms a group of its own. If you group the even and the odd bonds, you therefore need three groups, where one group per bond needs four. Fewer groups mean fewer factors, and also a shallower circuit: with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2` the two-qubit depth is 95 against 139. The lattice decides which bonds can share a group, which is why the partition is chosen here.\n"
msgstr "Pangalawa, isang pang-episyensiya: ang lahat ng on-site interaction term ay diagonal sa occupation basis at nagko-commute sa isa't isa, kaya maaari silang magbahagi ng iisang group at i-synthesize nang magkakasama. Ganoon din para sa mga bond na hindi humahawak sa iisang site. Sa isang chain, bawat ikalawang bond ay ganoong set: ang mga bond 0 at 2 ay kumikilos sa magkahiwalay na pares ng mode, kaya nagko-commute ang mga hopping term nila at maaaring magbahagi ng group, at ang bond 1 ay bumubuo ng sarili nitong group. Kung igagrupo mo ang even at odd na bond, tatlong group ang kailangan mo, samantalang apat ang kailangan kung isang group kada bond. Mas kaunting group ay mas kaunting factor, at mas mababaw din na Circuit: sa Gray code na may `max_occupation = 2`, ang two-qubit depth ay 95 laban sa 139. Ang lattice ang nagpapasya kung aling mga bond ang maaaring magbahagi ng group, kaya dito pinipili ang partition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute carries that decision into the circuit: an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one sub-evolution per group. The partition is chosen at the bosonic level, while the lattice structure is still visible, and it survives untouched through the mapping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) covers the checks a grouping should pass.\n"
msgstr "Dinadala ng attribute na [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") ang desisyong iyon sa Circuit: ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate sa ibabaw ng grouped na operator ay nade-decompose sa isang sub-evolution kada group. Pinipili ang partition sa bosonic na antas, habang nakikita pa ang estruktura ng lattice, at nananatili itong buo sa buong mapping. Saklaw ng [gabay sa grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation) ang mga pagsusuring dapat pasado sa isang grouping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every group must itself be Hermitian, which is what the preceding pairing buys. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks all groups in one call:\n"
msgstr "Dapat Hermitian din ang bawat group, na siyang naibibigay ng naunang pagpapares. Sinusuri ng [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") ang lahat ng group sa isang tawag:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see what each group holds, separate the groups:\n"
msgstr "Para makita kung ano ang laman ng bawat group, paghiwalayin ang mga group:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The even-and-odd grouping is a choice, and the alternative is easy to measure. If you give every bond a group of its own, you need four groups, and the same circuit then costs more two-qubit depth. The depth is counted after the circuit is lowered with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2`, which step 4 explains:\n"
msgstr "Pagpili ang even-and-odd na grouping, at madaling sukatin ang alternatibo. Kung bibigyan mo ang bawat bond ng sarili nitong group, apat na group ang kailangan mo, at mas malaking two-qubit depth ang magagastos ng parehong Circuit. Binibilang ang depth pagkatapos ibaba ang Circuit gamit ang Gray code na may `max_occupation = 2`, na ipinapaliwanag ng hakbang 4:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-bosonic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. The bosonic circuit {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr "3. Ang bosonic Circuit {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note what is absent from the circuit. There is no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. It acts on four bosonic modes:\n"
msgstr "Pansinin kung ano ang wala sa Circuit. Walang truncation, walang encoding, at walang bilang ng qubit. Kumikilos ito sa apat na bosonic mode:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The wires are bosonic modes, not qubits. Note that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") takes **integers**, not flags: a mode can hold any number of bosons, so a Fock state is a list of occupation numbers.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga wire ay mga bosonic mode, hindi mga qubit. Tandaan na ang [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ay tumatanggap ng mga **integer**, hindi flag: ang isang mode ay maaaring maglaman ng kahit ilang boson, kaya ang Fock state ay listahan ng mga occupation number.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") turns the grouping from [step 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping) into one gate per group:\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng iisang [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") na isang gate kada group ang grouping mula sa [hakbang 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first group holds the bonds on modes 0 and 1 and on modes 2 and 3, so its gate spans all four modes, and so does the on-site group. The middle bond has a gate of its own on modes 1 and 2.\n"
msgstr "Ang unang group ay naglalaman ng mga bond sa mode 0 at 1 at sa mode 2 at 3, kaya sumasaklaw ang gate nito sa lahat ng apat na mode, at ganoon din ang on-site group. Ang gitnang bond ay may sariling gate sa mode 1 at 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Skip that decomposition and the grouping is simply ignored. Which method does the splitting is the `synthesis` of the gate, with [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") as the default; [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows the alternatives.\n"
msgstr "Kung lalaktawan ang decomposition na iyon, hindi papansinin ang grouping. Ang `synthesis` ng gate ang paraang gumagawa ng paghahati, na ang [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") ang default; ipinapakita ng [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) ang mga alternatibo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Choose the encoding at transpile time {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"
msgstr "4. Piliin ang encoding sa transpile time {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the payoff. The same circuit is lowered four times, under four different [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") values, by changing one argument. A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") pairs the encoding with the truncation of every mode, and the following preset derives the layout, the state preparation, and the operator mapping from that one spec (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). A string such as `\"gray\"` is accepted wherever a `LevelEncoding` is.\n"
msgstr "Narito ang bentahe. Ang parehong Circuit ay ibinababa nang apat na beses, sa ilalim ng apat na magkakaibang value ng [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\"), sa pamamagitan ng pagbabago ng isang argument. Ipinapares ng [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") ang encoding sa truncation ng bawat mode, at hinahango ng sumusunod na preset ang layout, ang state preparation, at ang operator mapping mula sa isang spec na iyon (tingnan ang [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). Tinatanggap ang string gaya ng `\"gray\"` saanman tinatanggap ang `LevelEncoding`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These numbers contradict a natural guess. The unary encodings use $d$ qubits per mode against $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ for the compact codes, and at $d = 3$ the compact codes win on both axes at once: fewer qubits and far fewer entangling gates. The two unary variants differ in the operator they emit, not in their layout: [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") carries a projector on every other qubit of a mode, which makes it the most expensive of the four to evolve, and [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") leaves the projectors out and agrees with it on the one-hot subspace. The [mappers guide](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) shows the two operators side by side, and explains why the Gray code beats standard binary (SB) on the hopping terms.\n"
msgstr "Sumasalungat ang mga numerong ito sa natural na hula. Gumagamit ang mga unary encoding ng $d$ qubit kada mode, kumpara sa $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ para sa mga compact code, at sa $d = 3$ nananalo ang mga compact code sa dalawang aspeto nang sabay: mas kaunting qubit at mas kaunting entangling gate. Magkaiba ang dalawang unary variant sa operator na ibinibigay nila, hindi sa layout nila: ang [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") ay may projector sa bawat ikalawang qubit ng isang mode, kaya ito ang pinakamahal i-evolve sa apat, at ang [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") ay walang projector at sumasang-ayon dito sa one-hot subspace. Ipinapakita ng [gabay sa mappers](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) ang dalawang operator nang magkatabi, at ipinapaliwanag kung bakit mas mahusay ang Gray code kaysa sa standard binary (SB) sa mga hopping term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sawaya et al. report the same ordering <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"
msgstr "Iniulat ni Sawaya et al. ang parehong pagkakasunod-sunod <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> though the unary code tends to require more qubits but fewer operations, it is often the case that the SB or Gray code is more efficient both in terms of qubit counts and operation counts\n"
msgstr "> bagaman ang unary code ay may tendensiyang mangailangan ng mas maraming qubit pero mas kaunting operasyon, madalas na ang SB o Gray code ay mas episyente pareho sa bilang ng qubit at sa bilang ng operasyon\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Their conclusion is that the best code depends on the Hamiltonian and on $d$, which is the strongest argument for not fixing the choice in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang konklusyon nila ay nakadepende ang pinakamahusay na code sa Hamiltonian at sa $d$, na siyang pinakamalakas na argumento para hindi ayusin ang pagpili sa Circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Under a level encoding a mode spans several qubits, so the qubit register is wider than the mode register. The preset uses [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), which derives the register width from the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) walks through the stages the preset runs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Sa ilalim ng level encoding, sumasaklaw ang isang mode sa ilang qubit, kaya mas malapad ang qubit register kaysa sa mode register. Gumagamit ang preset ng [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), na hinahango ang lapad ng register mula sa [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). Dinadaanan ng [gabay sa transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) ang mga yugtong pinapatakbo ng preset.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-against-exact-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Verify against exact dynamics {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"
msgstr "5. I-verify laban sa eksaktong dynamics {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "None of the preceding steps establishes that the circuit is right. For that, compare the site densities $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ after evolution against an exact reference computed on the encoded Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Wala sa mga naunang hakbang ang nagpapatunay na tama ang Circuit. Para doon, ihambing ang mga site density na $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ pagkatapos ng evolution laban sa eksaktong reference na kinalkula sa na-encode na Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference has to be computed in the same truncated space the circuit works in, because comparing against an untruncated calculation would conflate Trotter error with truncation error, which are different things and worth separating (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Dapat kalkulahin ang reference sa parehong truncated space na ginagamit ng Circuit, dahil ang paghahambing sa untruncated na kalkulasyon ay maghahalo sa Trotter error at truncation error, na magkaibang bagay at sulit paghiwalayin (tingnan ang [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With those in hand, the exact evolution in the truncated space:\n"
msgstr "Taglay ang mga iyon, ang eksaktong evolution sa truncated space:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bosons spread from the occupied end of the chain towards the empty one, and the two bosons are conserved:\n"
msgstr "Kumakalat ang mga boson mula sa okupadong dulo ng chain patungo sa walang laman, at napapanatili ang dalawang boson:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the circuit. Note that the preceding reference was built from `initial` directly, so the circuit compared against it must contain only the evolution, because the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate would re-prepare a state that is already prepared.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, ang Circuit. Pansinin na ang naunang reference ay binuo mula sa `initial` nang direkta, kaya ang Circuit na ikinukumpara dito ay dapat naglalaman lang ng evolution, dahil ang gate na [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ay muling maghahanda ng state na nakahanda na.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error halves as the step count doubles, which is the $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ signature of a first-order product formula. That is the evidence that the discrepancy is Trotter error and the encoding is faithful.\n"
msgstr "Nagiging kalahati ang error kapag dinoble ang bilang ng step, na siyang pirma ng $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ ng isang first-order product formula. Iyan ang ebidensya na Trotter error ang pagkakaiba at tapat ang encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The repetitions come from the `synthesis` of the gate, which Trotterizes in bosonic space where the grouping still exists: each step applies every group once, and the steps follow one another. That is different from handing a [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) with `reps > 1` to the qubit-level synthesis plugin. There, each group is already its own [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), so the formula only subdivides the terms within a group and never interleaves the groups. The groups do not mutually commute, so that leaves a single outer Trotter step whose error does not shrink however large `reps` is. [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) compares the two and covers higher orders.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Ang mga pag-uulit ay nagmumula sa `synthesis` ng gate, na nagta-Trotterize sa bosonic space kung saan umiiral pa ang grouping: bawat step ay naglalapat ng bawat group nang isang beses, at sunud-sunod ang mga step. Iba iyon sa pagbibigay ng [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) na may `reps > 1` sa qubit-level synthesis plugin. Doon, ang bawat group ay sarili nang [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), kaya hinahati lang ng formula ang mga term sa loob ng isang group at hindi kailanman pinagsasalitan ang mga group. Hindi nagko-commute ang mga group sa isa't isa, kaya nag-iiwan ito ng iisang outer Trotter step na ang error ay hindi lumiliit gaano man kalaki ang `reps`. Ikinukumpara ng [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) ang dalawa at saklaw ang mas mataas na order.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The preceding [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) call is essential. [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) uses a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s exact definition and bypasses the product formula entirely. If you verify against an un-decomposed circuit, you see near-perfect agreement even for a deliberately wrong synthesis. The un-decomposed circuit also forces a dense $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$ operator to be built, whereas a decomposed circuit applies gates one at a time. Other simulators can treat the gate differently, so this check depends on the simulator, whereas hardware always needs the decomposed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Babala\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Mahalaga ang naunang tawag sa [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose). Ginagamit ng [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) ang eksaktong definition ng isang [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) at llumalampas sa product formula. Kung magve-verify ka laban sa Circuit na hindi decomposed, makikita mo ang halos perpektong pagsang-ayon kahit sa sadyang maling synthesis. Pinipilit din ng un-decomposed na Circuit na bumuo ng siksik na $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$ na operator, samantalang ang decomposed na Circuit ay naglalapat ng mga gate nang isa-isa. Maaaring iba ang pagtrato ng ibang simulator sa gate, kaya nakadepende sa simulator ang pagsusuring ito, samantalang laging kailangan ng hardware ang decomposed na anyo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the central check: the physics must not depend on which encoding was chosen.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, ang sentral na pagsusuri: hindi dapat nakadepende ang physics sa kung aling encoding ang pinili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qubit counts, Pauli structures, and circuit depths all differ, and the physics agrees to ten decimal places. The encoding is an implementation choice, which is why it belongs to the transpiler. The two unary variants agree here because the simulated state stays on the one-hot subspace; away from it they would differ.\n"
msgstr "Magkakaiba ang bilang ng qubit, ang mga Pauli structure, at ang mga depth ng Circuit, at nagkakasundo ang physics hanggang sampung decimal place. Ang encoding ay pagpili sa implementasyon, kaya ito ay nabibilang sa Transpiler. Nagkakasundo rito ang dalawang unary variant dahil nananatili ang na-simulate na state sa one-hot subspace; sa labas nito ay magkakaiba sila.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Truncation is a convergence parameter {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"
msgstr "6. Ang truncation ay isang convergence parameter {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final step is specific to bosons. Everything so far had fixed `max_occupation = 2`, that is $d = 3$. However, the truncation is not a free choice: it is a **convergence parameter**, and an answer is only trustworthy after it stops moving (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Ang huling hakbang ay partikular sa mga boson. Sa lahat ng nauna, nakatakda ang `max_occupation = 2`, ibig sabihin $d = 3$. Gayunpaman, hindi malayang pagpili ang truncation: ito ay isang **convergence parameter**, at mapagkakatiwalaan lang ang sagot kapag tumigil na itong gumalaw (tingnan ang [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit carries no truncation, so the circuit itself does not change when the cutoff does: only the transpilation is repeated. What changes is the size of what comes out, and a sweep is only as cheap as it is here because the system is tiny. The following reference is an exact classical simulation of the truncated dynamics, which is possible for four sites and grows exponentially with the number of qubits. For a problem beyond that reach there is no exact reference to compare against, and the convergence has to be judged by other means.\n"
msgstr "Walang truncation ang Circuit, kaya hindi nagbabago ang Circuit mismo kapag nagbago ang cutoff: ang transpilation lang ang inuulit. Ang nagbabago ay ang laki ng lumalabas, at ang sweep ay mura lang dito dahil napakaliit ng sistema. Ang sumusunod na reference ay isang eksaktong classical simulation ng truncated dynamics, na posible para sa apat na site at lumalaki nang exponential kasabay ng bilang ng qubit. Para sa problemang lampas sa abot nito, walang eksaktong reference na mapaghahambingan, at kailangang husgahan ang convergence sa ibang paraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$) each site holds at most one boson, so the interaction term, which needs two on a site, cannot act at all, and the densities are off by about $7 \\times 10^{-4}$. When you add the third level, the result captures the interaction, and from `max_occupation = 3` on the result is stationary to machine precision: converged.\n"
msgstr "Sa `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$), isang boson lang ang kayang hawakan ng bawat site, kaya hindi talaga makakilos ang interaction term, na nangangailangan ng dalawa sa isang site, at mali ng humigit-kumulang $7 \\times 10^{-4}$ ang mga density. Kapag idinagdag ang ikatlong level, nakukuha ng resulta ang interaksyon, at mula sa `max_occupation = 3` pataas ay stationary ang resulta hanggang machine precision: converged na.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reason that it stops at `max_occupation = 2` is particle number. The Hamiltonian conserves the number of bosons, and this state holds two, so no site can ever hold more than two, whatever the evolution time and whether the interaction is repulsive or attractive. If you evolve to $t = 6$ instead of $t = 0.4$, or flip the sign of $U$, the densities at `max_occupation = 2` and higher stay unchanged to $10^{-13}$.\n"
msgstr "Ang dahilan kung bakit tumitigil ito sa `max_occupation = 2` ay ang bilang ng particle. Iniingatan ng Hamiltonian ang bilang ng boson, at dalawa ang laman ng state na ito, kaya walang site na maaaring humawak ng higit sa dalawa, anuman ang evolution time at maging repulsive man o attractive ang interaksyon. Kung ie-evolve mo hanggang $t = 6$ sa halip na $t = 0.4$, o babaligtarin ang sign ng $U$, nananatiling hindi nagbabago ang mga density sa `max_occupation = 2` at mas mataas hanggang $10^{-13}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does push the requirement up is the **number of bosons**. Three bosons on the same chain change by about $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ between `max_occupation = 2` and `3` after the same short evolution, and by about $0.3$ after $t = 6$. That is a statement about this model and a conserved quantity, and it is a bound only for operators that conserve the particle number; it is not a general rule, so the cutoff has to be swept, not guessed.\n"
msgstr "Ang nagtutulak pataas ng requirement ay ang **bilang ng boson**. Ang tatlong boson sa parehong chain ay nagbabago ng humigit-kumulang $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ sa pagitan ng `max_occupation = 2` at `3` pagkatapos ng parehong maikling evolution, at ng humigit-kumulang $0.3$ pagkatapos ng $t = 6$. Pahayag iyan tungkol sa model na ito at sa isang conserved na dami, at bound lang ito para sa mga operator na nagpapanatili ng bilang ng particle; hindi ito pangkalahatang tuntunin, kaya kailangang i-sweep ang cutoff, hindi hulaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sweep has a price on the circuit side too, which is what the exact reference does not show. The same bosonic circuit, lowered with the Gray code at each cutoff:\n"
msgstr "May presyo rin ang sweep sa panig ng Circuit, na hindi ipinapakita ng eksaktong reference. Ang parehong bosonic Circuit, na ibinaba gamit ang Gray code sa bawat cutoff:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each extra level costs depth, and the qubit count jumps whenever $d$ passes a power of two. When you converge in $d$, you therefore trade accuracy against circuit size, so the sweep is more than a numerical check.\n"
msgstr "Bawat dagdag na level ay may gastos sa depth, at tumatalon ang bilang ng qubit kapag lumampas ang $d$ sa power ng dalawa. Kapag nag-converge ka sa $d$, ikinakalakal mo ang accuracy laban sa laki ng Circuit, kaya higit pa sa numerical check ang sweep.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that $d = 2$ being nearly right is a coincidence of the observable: the site *densities* barely move, while the underlying state is qualitatively wrong (it has no doubly-occupied component). If one observable converges, that does not show that another has converged.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin din na ang pagiging halos tama ng $d = 2$ ay nagkataon lang dahil sa observable: halos hindi gumagalaw ang mga site *density*, habang qualitatively mali ang pinagbabatayang state (wala itong doubly-occupied na component). Kung nag-converge ang isang observable, hindi ito nagpapatunay na nag-converge na ang iba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Ano ang dapat tandaan {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The encoding is a transpiler concern.** The bosonic circuit in [step 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile) mentions no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. Four encodings then lowered it to four different circuits, all reproducing the same physics. Nothing upstream of the transpiler had to change.\n"
msgstr "**Ang encoding ay usapin ng transpiler.** Walang binabanggit na truncation, encoding, o bilang ng qubit ang bosonic circuit sa [step 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile). Apat na encoding ang nag-lower nito sa apat na magkakaibang circuit, at pare-pareho ang physics na nai-reproduce ng lahat. Walang kailangang baguhin sa anumang nasa itaas ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**For bosons this is not merely convenient.** The truncation is a convergence parameter that has to be swept, and it lives inside the encoding. A circuit built against a fixed encoding would have to be rebuilt for every value of $d$.\n"
msgstr "**Para sa mga boson, hindi lang ito basta maginhawa.** Ang truncation ay isang convergence parameter na kailangang i-sweep, at nasa loob ito ng encoding. Ang circuit na binuo laban sa isang fixed na encoding ay kailangang buuin muli para sa bawat halaga ng $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping, and group for Hermiticity.** A single hopping term is not Hermitian and cannot be exponentiated; the bond pair on the hand is Hermitian and therefore can be exponentiated. Decide the partition at the bosonic level, where the lattice is still visible. That is physically necessary, and the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute exists to carry the decision forward.\n"
msgstr "**Mag-group bago mag-mapping, at mag-group para sa Hermiticity.** Ang isang hopping term ay hindi Hermitian at hindi maaaring i-exponentiate; ang bond pair sa kamay ay Hermitian kaya maaari itong i-exponentiate. Piliin ang partition sa bosonic level, kung saan nakikita pa ang lattice. Kailangan ito ayon sa physics, at ang [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute ay nariyan para dalhin pasulong ang desisyong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Do not assume the low-weight encoding is the cheap one.** At $d = 3$ the compact codes beat both unary variants on qubits and gates simultaneously, and the projected variant is the costliest of all. Measure; the crossover is $d$-dependent.\n"
msgstr "**Huwag ipagpalagay na ang low-weight encoding ang mura.** Sa $d = 3$, mas mahusay ang mga compact code kaysa sa parehong unary variant pagdating sa qubit at gate nang sabay, at ang projected variant ang pinakamahal sa lahat. Sukatin mo; nakadepende sa $d$ ang crossover.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Truncation breaks the algebra, in a quantifiable way.** Only on the top retained level, by $d$. That is also why mapping does not commute with normal ordering.\n"
msgstr "**Sinisira ng truncation ang algebra, sa paraang masusukat.** Sa pinakamataas na retained level lang, ng $d$. Kaya rin hindi nagko-commute ang mapping sa normal ordering.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend this example. If you replace the chain’s edge list with the bonds of a square lattice, you need no other change, because the `bose_hubbard` function defined earlier is already geometry-agnostic. A custom encoding of your own (a block-unary code, for example, which interpolates between unary and compact) also plugs in through the same `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` seam the preset uses.\n"
msgstr "May dalawang direksyon para palawakin ang halimbawang ito. Kung papalitan mo ang edge list ng chain ng mga bond ng isang square lattice, wala ka nang ibang babaguhin, dahil geometry-agnostic na ang `bose_hubbard` function na dinefine kanina. Ang sarili mong custom na encoding (halimbawa, isang block-unary code, na nag-iinterpolate sa pagitan ng unary at compact) ay maisasaksak din sa parehong `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` seam na ginagamit ng preset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Design principles of operator representations](operators#operators-explanation) explains the operator data structure behind the Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ng [Mga prinsipyo ng disenyo ng mga representasyon ng operator](operators#operators-explanation) ang data structure ng operator sa likod ng Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation) covers the encodings and writing a mapper of your own.\n"
msgstr "Sinasaklaw ng [I-map ang mga representasyon ng operator](mappers#mappers-explanation) ang mga encoding at ang pagsulat ng sarili mong mapper.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) walks through the stages the preset runs.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng [I-transpile ang mga bosonic circuit](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) ang mga stage na pinapatakbo ng preset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows how to reduce the Trotter error in bosonic space.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng [Mag-synthesize ng Evolution gate sa bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) kung paano bawasan ang Trotter error sa bosonic space.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Every depth reported is on an abstract, fully connected register. Mapping to real hardware connectivity is a separate stage, and an occupation encoding’s per-mode qubit blocks give a router rather different structure to work with than one qubit per mode.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Ang bawat iniulat na depth ay nasa abstract at fully connected na register. Ang pag-map sa tunay na hardware connectivity ay hiwalay na stage, at ang mga per-mode na bloke ng qubit ng isang occupation encoding ay nagbibigay sa router ng medyo ibang estruktura kaysa sa isang qubit bawat mode.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

